This section will collect editable RevealJS slide decks that can be taught directly or adapted for different audiences.
Each deck should include:

source .qmd files rather than only a rendered presentation;
learning outcomes and an approximate duration;
speaker or facilitator notes where appropriate;
attribution and licences for externally sourced material;
links to associated exercises, datasets and modules.

Use the slide-deck template on GitHub as a starting point.

This section will contain small, documented datasets suitable for teaching evidence-synthesis methods.
Contributed datasets should include:

a clear licence and source;
a data dictionary;
enough context to understand the teaching example;
a distinction between original, simulated and modified data;
scripts documenting any cleaning or transformation;
no sensitive or personally identifying information.

Simulated data are welcome when they make an assumption or statistical behaviour easier to see.
